--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (1/4 key facts kept) ---
I read in the evening paper that more than two and a half million workers were out of employment, and that the coal and cotton trades were in dispute; gloomily I thought of Bert and wondered how he would fare among so many competitors for a job.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (3/4 key facts kept) ---
I entered the correct total in the ledger (5115).

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
I read in The Times that the New Year opens gloomily, that more than two and a half million persons are out of work, and that the coal and cotton trades are in dispute.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that she was in a land flowing with milk and honey, where there was abundance of food for all.

