--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the evening paper that Princess Louise, the King's eldest sister, was dead; and that she had been seriously ill for some months. I was sorry to hear it.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald: Death of the Princess Royal, London, Football, Millwall beat Charlton by six goals to nil.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
read in The Times the death of Princess Louise; and read also that she had been seriously ill for some months, with a recurrence of heart trouble.
