--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Wednesday, the 7th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the evening paper that almost every day in the first weeks of the New Year is inaugural day somewhere in the United States, as new governors take the oath of office in 33 states, and recalled Democratic victories at the last election; I read that the big seaplane Do-X is scheduled to start a transatlantic flight to America on January 20; and I read that the Prince of Wales and Prince George are to sail for South America on January 17.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Wednesday, the 7th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald of almost every day being inaugural day somewhere in the United States during the first weeks of the new year, as governors in 33 states take the oath of office; I read of the advent of new administrations in many states recalling Democratic victories of the election in November, and I felt glad that the Democrats had won.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Wednesday, the 7th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
1. Read in The Times of almost every day being inaugural day somewhere in the United States during the first weeks of the New Year, as governors in 33 states take the oath of office.
